From 74bca85b0082362df80166651021dff8101a93b1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 01:05:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] perf(client): a chunk that has arrived renders in the page's
 own commit

React.lazy suspends a part once even when its chunk has loaded (its promise
answers only in a microtask), and React then holds the commit that reveals
it until 300 ms after its fallback showed: the computer's game page (and the
lobby's arrival with it) and a joined game's board came up about 300 ms late
on every load. lazyChunk now hands its lazy a thenable that answers as it is
asked once the chunk is in, so the part renders at once; before, it
suspends as it did. The type stays one lazy (retry still makes a fresh one).

